# Structured INFO values, bound to the node that identifies record and key.
#
# The census counts INFO value nodes and the record digest covers the raw INFO
# string, but neither notices a structured value that disagrees with the key it
# was parsed from. Hashing the value together with its own IRI closes that, and
# because the result is a histogram it needs no ordering guarantee from the
# engine - GROUP_CONCAT would not be portable here.
SELECT ?bucket (COUNT(*) AS ?valueCount)
